---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, REVIEW_CYCLE_MONTHS } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
import { P } from '../../lib/engine/params';
import { seuilRegroupement } from '../../lib/engine/famille';
import { formatMoney } from '../../lib/format';
const e = (n: number, d = 0) => formatMoney(n, d, lang);
---
<PageLayout title="Editorial policy Mon Titre de Séjour: sources, tests and corrections" description="Where the amounts and rules on this site about foreign nationals in France come from, why we publish no prefecture waiting times and how an error gets corrected." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Editorial policy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Editorial policy and corrections</h1>
    <p>A permit refused because the renewal was filed late, a stamp bought for the wrong amount, a citizenship file sent three months too early: in these procedures, guesswork costs months. These are our rules.</p>
    <h2>Responsibility</h2><p>{AUTHOR_NAME} is responsible for content and calculations. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    <h2>Official sources only</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Service-Public.fr</strong> pages (published by the French legal and administrative information directorate), with the date each was checked;</li>
      <li>the <strong>CESEDA</strong> (immigration code), the <strong>Civil Code</strong> and the <strong>2026 Finance Act</strong>, cited by article;</li>
      <li>orders published in the <strong>Official Journal</strong> (minimum wage, reference salary for the talent passport);</li>
      <li>the <strong>minimum wage</strong> series published by Insee.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What we will not publish</h2><p>No average prefecture times, no approval rates and no "tips" for getting an appointment: no official source supports them. No amount is published unless it was read on a dated official page.</p>
    <h2>No commercial interest</h2><p>We receive nothing from lawyers, appointment platforms or language schools, and name none of them.</p>
    <h2>Tests</h2><p>Before each release, automated tests replay the examples on the official pages: {e(P.tarifs.normal.premiere)} and {e(P.tarifs.normal.renouvellement)} for an employee card, {e(seuilRegroupement(4, '2027-06-15').seuil, 2)} for family reunification with four people once all twelve months are at today's minimum wage, {P.naturalisation.delai_mois} months to answer a naturalisation. Any difference blocks publication.</p>
    <h2>Review cycle</h2><p>At least every {REVIEW_CYCLE_MONTHS} months, after every Finance Act, every minimum-wage increase and every update of a page we cite.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <ol><li>Check against the official source.</li><li>Fix the parameter or calculation, add a test.</li><li>New date on the page.</li></ol>
    <p>See also the <a href={route('method', lang)}>method page</a>. Version: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
